# port-patches.sh: glm/r8b @ 70fd9f5b8d6d over glm/zig-engine-fixes-on-186 @ e027c49cd06d (commits 069c49ffd2dc..1ea862b590e4); regenerate with scripts/port-patches.sh, do not edit
glm_cuda: spill v2 with KV sharding: each rank keeps and restores its own view of a kept state under its home part (port of GLM 0118's spill blocks)

With KV sharding a kept state's latent rows are only on the rank that owned
its stream (its home part); every other section is on both ranks. Spill v2 of
such states, so TF_GLM_SPILL_V2=1 and TF_GLM_KV_SHARD=1 run together (the
refusal of the pair goes).

- cuda_spill_state: an owner-sharded layout: the home part's owner stores a
  token's latent and pooled rows (6,204 bytes), the other rank the pooled
  rows alone (396), so a pair stores a point's blocks in 6,600 bytes a token
  instead of 12,408; the lineage is salted with the home part (a carried
  conversation names new blocks, never another part's), the point records
  its home, the namespace and the fingerprint say owner_sharded.
- cuda_spill_tier: rank 0 keeps its view with the salted lineage and the
  keep note carries it; rank 1 checks its own state's home against the note
  before it writes its view. A restore reads the point's part from rank 0's
  store and sends it in has (a rank answers present only for that part, else
  every rank forgets the point); each rank's destination is its own view
  with the home recorded, and the resume then places it as any kept state
  (in its part, moved home, carried, or from 0). A restore whose resume
  could only start from 0 (its home part full, no carry) does not start
  (KvShardHomeFull, asked before the cache makes room and before any read):
  its prompt prefills at once, also beside other restores in flight.
- Points per part (points_part0, points_part1) in every rank's tier counters
  on /health and /metrics.

Switches: TF_GLM_SPILL_V2=1 (with --spill-gib and --snapshot-dir) together
with TF_GLM_KV_SHARD=1; each alone is unchanged except two zero counters a
rank under spill v2 alone and two more index lookups a restore (the stats
answer carries 36 counters instead of 34; one build on both ranks). Each
rank's store limits count its own bytes, so when points lean to one part that
part's owner reaches its cap first.

Tests (host): the owner-sharded layout, lineage, home and fingerprint
(cuda_spill_state, cuda_spill_identity), the store's per-part sizes, and the
tier over the two-rank host rig with both on (keep, restore into the home, has
naming the part, a rank missing or of the other part, restart, the
KvShardHomeFull refusal), each failing without its change.

Measured on the pair: not run yet (round 3; the next GPU session). Round 2's
image refused the pair at start on both ranks with the intended message (g2),
which this patch removes.

Credits: Robert Wojciechowski (GitHub @wojo, X @rwojo); spill v2's block store
design (2,048-token blocks, lineage, the write-at-keep ring, release and fsync
order): BadAd84 (https://github.com/BadAd84),
MiaAI-Lab/GLM-5.3-Flash-EXL3-2x-DGX-Sparks-TensorFold#118; GLM patches 0110
and 0118, MiaAI-Lab/GLM-5.3-Flash-EXL3-2x-DGX-Sparks-TensorFold#124 and #152.
Apply from the checkout root with: git apply 0023-zig-glm-spill-kv-shard.patch

